Dear David,

Following the recent re-tender process for the ATU-100, I am pleased to inform you that LNDE has been awarded the contract for NDE services at the Hamilton Plant. We look forward to David Park and the rest of the team beginning work on the upcoming scope.

Please note that all future ultrasonic thickness measurements on A312 TP316 lines must strictly adhere to stainless-steel velocity settings. This award follows the rejection of data under QSCP-NCR-2013-019, where carbon-steel velocity was incorrectly applied to 3-RF-101 and 2-RF-102. Corrective re-measurement of these reflux lines is a priority.

Regards,  Douglas Ferreira

Douglas Ferreira, Inspection Supervisor, API 570 inspector, QSCP Hamilton Inspection Department